{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1427","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Unshuffling a Deck"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a deck of $$$n$$$ cards numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ (not necessarily in this order in the deck). You have to sort the deck by repeating the following operation. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$2 \\le k \\le n$$$ and split the deck in $$$k$$$ nonempty contiguous parts $$$D_1, D_2,\\dots, D_k$$$ ($$$D_1$$$ contains the first $$$|D_1|$$$ cards of the deck, $$$D_2$$$ contains the following $$$|D_2|$$$ cards and so on). Then reverse the order of the parts, transforming the deck into $$$D_k, D_{k-1}, \\dots, D_2, D_1$$$ (so, the first $$$|D_k|$$$ cards of the new deck are $$$D_k$$$, the following $$$|D_{k-1}|$$$ cards are $$$D_{k-1}$$$ and so on). The internal order of each packet of cards $$$D_i$$$ is unchanged by the operation. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to obtain a sorted deck (i.e., a deck where the first card is $$$1$$$, the second is $$$2$$$ and so on) performing at most $$$n$$$ operations. It can be proven that it is always possible to sort the deck performing at most $$$n$$$ operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples of operation:"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" The following are three examples of valid operations (on three decks with different sizes). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If the deck is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[3 6 2 1 4 5 7]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (so $$$3$$$ is the first card and $$$7$$$ is the last card), we may apply the operation with $$$k=4$$$ and $$$D_1=$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[3 6]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$D_2=$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[2 1 4]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$D_3=$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[5]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$D_4=$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[7]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Doing so, the deck becomes "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[7 5 2 1 4 3 6]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If the deck is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[3 1 2]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", we may apply the operation with $$$k=3$$$ and $$$D_1=$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[3]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$D_2=$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[1]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$D_3=$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[2]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Doing so, the deck becomes "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[2 1 3]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If the deck is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[5 1 2 4 3 6]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", we may apply the operation with $$$k=2$$$ and $$$D_1=$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[5 1]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$D_2=$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[2 4 3 6]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Doing so, the deck becomes "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[2 4 3 6 5 1]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1\\le n\\le 52$$$)  — the number of cards in the deck."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$c_1, c_2, \\dots, c_n$$$  — the cards in the deck. The first card is $$$c_1$$$, the second is $$$c_2$$$ and so on."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that for all $$$i=1,\\dots,n$$$ there is exactly one $$$j\\in\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$$$ such that $$$c_j = i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On the first line, print the number $$$q$$$ of operations you perform (it must hold $$$0\\le q\\le n$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then, print $$$q$$$ lines, each describing one operation."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To describe an operation, print on a single line the number $$$k$$$ of parts you are going to split the deck in, followed by the size of the $$$k$$$ parts: $$$|D_1|, |D_2|, \\dots , |D_k|$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It must hold $$$2\\le k\\le n$$$, and $$$|D_i|\\ge 1$$$ for all $$$i=1,\\dots,k$$$, and $$$|D_1|+|D_2|+\\cdots + |D_k| = n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be proven that it is always possible to sort the deck performing at most $$$n$$$ operations. If there are several ways to sort the deck you can output any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n3 1 2 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n3 1 2 1\n2 1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n6 5 4 3 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n6 1 1 1 1 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Explanation of the first testcase:"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" Initially the deck is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[3 1 2 4]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The first operation splits the deck as "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[(3) (1 2) (4)]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and then transforms it into "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[4 1 2 3]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The second operation splits the deck as "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[(4) (1 2 3)]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and then transforms it into "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[1 2 3 4]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Explanation of the second testcase:"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" Initially the deck is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[6 5 4 3 2 1]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The first (and only) operation splits the deck as "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[(6) (5) (4) (3) (2) (1)]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and then transforms it into "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[1 2 3 4 5 6]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1427D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1427/problem/D"}